2. **Read-only means read-only.** The closed list of `az` verbs, as a property first: `account show`, `group exists|list`, `webapp list|show|config show|config appsettings list` (value hashes only; never print a value; the settings list is not needed except `alwaysOn`, so prefer `webapp config show --query alwaysOn`), `resource list|show`, `sql db show|list`, `sql server show`, `monitor activity-log list`, `monitor metrics list|list-definitions`, `monitor diagnostic-settings list`, `monitor log-analytics query`, `monitor app-insights query`, `account get-access-token` (for the Kudu GET only). **Any other verb: prove it only reads, or STOP.** Never `create|update|set|delete|restart|stop|start|deploy|pause|resume|log config|identity assign|role assignment`; never enable logging to get a log; never `--yes`.
3. **Never touch what the ruling does not name.** No HTTP to anything but, if slot 5 allows, the one `/health/ready` GET of step 4. Never `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `2_Project_Files/HP Docs/`, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/`, `.local/`, `4_Credentials/inbound_with_secrets`, `.tools/backup-*`. The HP design-system material is access-controlled: never search for, fetch or quote it.
4. **Never delete** (`rm`, `rmdir`, `az ... delete`); quarantine by MOVE to `.tools/b991/_quarantine/`. Other seats' trees: only files this brief names, by name, read-only (`.tools/b971/kit/identity_pass.sh`, `.tools/b971/kit/platlog971.zsh` as a pattern for the Kudu read, `.tools/b971/presig-uat0/resources-uat.txt`).
5. **No message to any human**; nothing to HP; no Jira write (Tuesday owns every Jira and records line). No person's name or e-mail in STATUS ("the product owner"). The hosted sites hold synthetic data only: print no customer content beyond counts and route names. The product owner's click is a fact of the diagnosis; his words are quoted only as in the header of this brief.
6. **Secrets:** never on argv (the Kudu token goes to `curl` on stdin as a config line), never printed, never in a kept file, STATUS or log excerpt; gitleaks over `.tools/b991/` and the evidence folder with a `ghp_`-shaped in-memory canary that fires (rc 1), the real scan rc 0; the 64-character base64 shape scan with an in-memory canary found, the real scan 0. Host names stay out of the evidence (`azurewebsites.net`, `scm.`, `vault.azure.net` 0; control 1).
7. **Shell:** never type `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; brace variables next to a `:`; no unquoted word starting with `=`; the Bash tool is zsh (use `pipestatus` or `bash -c`); macOS has no `timeout`.
8. **Records and code: none in this seat.** STATUS and evidence only; no commit, no push, no branch, no PR, no code edit, no record edit, no CI run.
9. **STATUS-NOW and files:** `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-31_B991_STATUS.md`, evidence `.../2026-10-31_B991_evidence/` (log and metric excerpts only: no screenshots are needed), kit `.tools/b991/`. Every number carries its instrument and a control that can fail; every census names its frame; a zero is a suspect until its control fired.

